      "Lyonel's younger son, born with a clubbed foot that excludes him from the martial career his family and his era both expect of a lord's son, Larys compensates with an entirely different set of talents — patience, observation, and an instinct for finding and keeping other people's secrets that eventually makes him, in all but formal title, master of whisperers.",
      "Where his brother Harwin trades in strength, Larys trades in leverage, cultivating a network of informants and collecting debts of information that he spends with exquisite timing throughout the war's political maneuvering — a man who understands, better than almost anyone else at court, that knowing a secret is worth considerably more than acting on it immediately.",
